>> title: Smoked Bologna
>> category: Smoked & Grilled
>> tags: bologna, barbecue, smoker, cheap cut, glaze
>> counters: Smokehouse
>> aka: barbecue bologna, barbeque bologna, bbq bologna, Oklahoma prime rib, bologna steak, smoked baloney
>> servings: 8
>> time: 4 hr 15 min
>> slack: forgiving — the thirty minutes setting the glaze is the only part that burns, and it burns because the glaze is sugar
>> pairs-with: hush-puppies

Bring the #smoker{} to 250°F (120°C) over hickory and hold it there.

>> step: score in a diamond, coat
Peel the casing off @beef bologna{3%lb}(1.35 kg; one whole chub), score it 1/4-in deep in a diamond pattern all over, and coat it with @yellow mustard{2%Tbs}, @dark brown sugar{2%Tbs}, @smoked paprika{1%Tbs}, @coarse black pepper{2%tsp}, and @garlic powder{1%tsp}.

>> step: smoke 250°F (120°C) 3 hr
Smoke @&(~1)scored bologna{} for ~smoke{3%hr}, until the cuts have opened and the outside has gone dark and dry to the touch.

>> step: stir a glaze
Stir @barbecue sauce{1/2%cup}(120 mL) with @dark brown sugar{1%Tbs} and @cider vinegar{1%Tbs} until it brushes on thin.

>> step: brush, set 30 min, rest 10 min, slice thick
Brush @&(~1)glaze{} over @&(~2)smoked bologna{} and return it to the smoker until it sets and turns tacky, ~smoke{30%min}, then ~rest{10%min} and cut it into 1/2-in slabs.
